# NOTE: `dist/` is intentionally NOT gitignored. The built React shell must
# ship with the canonical commit so Databricks Apps git-source mode (Option B
# zero-config install) can serve the frontend without running `npm install` /
# Vite build inside the Apps build container. The Apps platform's npm proxy
# is unreliable, so we avoid touching it entirely. Pre-built artifacts are
# committed as part of every release; `./scripts/deploy.sh` and
# `./vibe2value` verify `dist/index.html` is present and fresh before push.

# `package.json` + `package-lock.json` are NOT committed. The Databricks Apps
# build runner detects `package.json` at the repo root and unconditionally
# runs `npm install` (which then fails against the platform's internal npm
# proxy: `npm-proxy.dev.databricks.com`). Since we ship the pre-built `dist/`
# directly, npm install is unnecessary at deploy time -- and per the Apps
# docs, "If you omit package.json from the app root, Databricks won't run
# npm at all." Templates (`package.json.template`, `package-lock.json.template`)
# are committed so local developers can `cp package.json.template package.json
# && npm install` (or `./vibe2value install`) to set up a dev environment.
package.json
package-lock.json

